repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/jmouchotte-Onepoint/Text-To-Query-Qecurity-EventB
abstract: >-
  Event-B formal model verifying, before execution, that a dynamically
  built query is structurally consistent, secure, and authorized for the
  requesting user and the current data context. Six machines (M1-M6)
  introduce structural, security, and data-centric authorization
  requirements progressively; authorization is derived at each execution
  from data metadata, user attributes, and execution context. All 137
  proof obligations are discharged in Rodin. The model is agnostic to the
  query generator and is instantiated on relational and non-relational
  engines (SQL, MongoDB, Cassandra).
keywords:
  - formal methods
  - Event-B
  - Rodin
  - query validation
  - data security
  - access control
  - text-to-query
  - database systems
